# EchoChamber — Complete Project Walkthrough (Interview Guide)

> Read this top-to-bottom once. You'll be able to explain every part of this project to an interviewer.

---

## 🧠 What is EchoChamber? (The 30-Second Pitch)

EchoChamber is a **real-time group chat application** where every user has a **personality identity**.

When you sign up, you take a 5-question quiz. Based on your answers the system assigns you:
- A **personality profile** (traits like `analytical`, `introvert`, `night`, etc.)
- A **unique color** (derived from your answer sum)
- A **unique avatar shape** (circle, triangle, square, hexagon, star)

Then you join chat rooms, and your avatar + color appear next to every message you send. It's not just "username + text" — it's identity-aware chat.

**Tech stack in one sentence:** React (Vite) frontend → Node.js/Express + Socket.io backend → Supabase (Postgres + Auth) as the database → Upstash Redis as the cache + real-time layer.

